==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|ang|non|þræll}} (Danish {{m|da|træl}}, Swedish {{m|sv|träl}}), perhaps from Proto-Norse ''*þrāhilaʀ'', from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*þragilaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrahilaz}}, ''*þrēhilaz'', from ''*þreh-'', ''*þreg-'', ''*þrag-'' ‘to run’, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*trāgʰ-||pull, drag, race, run}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θɹæːl/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=þrǣl|m}}

# a [[slave]], someone beholden to a [[lord]] or [[master]]

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|thral}}, {{l|enm|thralle}}, {{l|enm|threl}}, {{l|enm|threlle}}
** English: {{l|en|thrall}}